\DOC CONCRETIZE_F_EVENTS_TAC

\TYPE {CONCRETIZE_F_EVENTS_TAC : term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Refines a single existentially quantified function unknown in the goal's
conclusion by substituting a supplied skeleton term for it, leaving the
skeleton's free function symbols as the new existential variables.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {concrete_f_events : term} is a lambda abstraction giving the
concrete shape to use for the existentially quantified witness; its free
(unbound) function variables become the new existential variables of the
resulting goal. Applied to a goal whose conclusion is {?f. t}, where the body
applies {f} to some arguments, the tactic replaces every application of {f} in
{t} by the skeleton applied to the same arguments and beta-reduced, giving {u},
and binds existentially the free function variables {x1 ... xn} of the
skeleton, in the order they appear:
{
       A ?- ?f. t
       ================================  CONCRETIZE_F_EVENTS_TAC concrete_f_events
       A ?- ?x1 ... xn. u
}
\noindent The rest of the conclusion, including the universal quantifiers and
hypotheses inside it, is unchanged.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces only this one transformation occurs, always on goals
whose conclusion is a single existential over a function later applied inside
the body.

\ENDDOC
